  "schema:name": "TrustDemoOnesaImmunization",
  "dcterms:title": "Onesa: dose on the national schedule",
  "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J3 and after. These are the Taifafeki birth doses once the district clinic has verified them, and every dose given in Onesa.\n\nWhy: the Onesan schedule engine works on Onesan EPI codes, so each dose must carry one. A dose that came from abroad keeps the issuer's product code beside the Onesan one, added through the ConceptMap and confirmed by the nurse. Nothing the other country said is overwritten. A verified foreign dose is recorded from its primary source, the signing hospital, and its Provenance says how it was verified.",
